<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>Giang Vo by Motorbike: Motorbike Parking Guide in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Giang Vo is Ba Dinh&rsquo;s event quarter, the boulevard-and-exhibition stretch between the landmark city and the working west, and its parking is a tidy version of the centre&rsquo;s with one honest exception stitched through it, the calendar. On ordinary days the quarter&rsquo;s frontages, hotels, offices and residential blocks, offer the calmest curb-side life this side of the river, and on event days the exhibition ground&rsquo;s arrivals change whole blocks at a stroke, which makes the Giang Vo rider&rsquo;s single most useful habit a question asked in the morning rather than a spot memorised at midnight. This guide reads the quarter&rsquo;s parking habits without inventing a single guaranteed spot, because parking in Hanoi is a local fact, not a page&rsquo;s promise.</p>
<p>The rental counter is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the river, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, and the desk&rsquo;s current pointers are part of the plan. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, browse the wider <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>, read the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/ba-dinh-parking-guide/">Ba Dinh parking guide</a> for the district-wide picture, and see the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/dong-da-parking-guide/">Dong Da parking guide</a> for the working district to the south.</p>
